# Pairs with KeepPolicyHonoured. Production as 10.2.0 shipped it: a
# republish kept the backup's original capture time, the only time the
# pass ranked by. A backup captured again just now therefore ranked as old,
# and the next pass under max-age (or keep-last, if a different backup had
# been captured in between) pruned the backup the capture had just
# returned. The mutation drops the ranking refresh from the register.
MODULE: KeepPolicyHonouredStaleRank
TARGET: KeepPolicyHonoured
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: a republish keeps its stale ranking time
PERTURBS: Register

--- FIND
          /\ Refresh(c)
          /\ cap' = [cap EXCEPT ![c] = [ph |-> "idle", id |-> 0, t |-> 0]]
--- REPLACE
          \* MUTATION: the ranking time is not refreshed.
          /\ lpt' = [lpt EXCEPT ![cap[c].id] = IF @ < cap[c].t THEN cap[c].t ELSE @]
          /\ UNCHANGED meta
          /\ cap' = [cap EXCEPT ![c] = [ph |-> "idle", id |-> 0, t |-> 0]]
--- END
